      "title": "brdwlk: Fix a field size (and signed overflow)",
      "message": "brdwlk: Fix a field size (and signed overflow)\n\nThe original packet length field cannot be four bytes long (with\nno bitmask), because that runs into the already dissected error\nand eof fields in the next two octets. It also only contains a\nvalue between 12 and 528. Shorten it to 2 bytes, so it cannot\noverflow when multiplied by 4 to convert from words to bytes.\n\nUse the original packet length in the case of truncation as a\nreported length for the subset passed to FC.\n\nAlso, in FC, fix a case of signed overflow caused by the least\nexpected integer promotion rule in C - the one that converts both\noperands of bitwise shift, such that an unsigned LHS smaller than\nan int is converted to a [signed] int.\n\nOSS-Fuzz 458867039\n",
